<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17281" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex-sufflo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exuf-</span></b> ), āre, v. a.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To blow away</i>, <i><span class="en">Cael.
				Aur. Tard. 4, 3, 57</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Agg. 1,
				9</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To blow at</i> or <i>upon</i> a
			person or thing (eccl. Lat.), <i><span class="en">Tert. Idol. 11
					<i>fin.</i></span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">radios igneos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Sir. 43, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">infantes (as a charm against the devil),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aug.
					Ep. 105 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quem (daemonem) eminus exsufflans, se
					exsufflari existimans, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sulp. Sev. Dial. 3, 8</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
